1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d4 Bb4 5. Nxe5 Qe7 6. Qd3 Nxe5 7. dxe5 Qxe5 8. Bd2 O-O 9. O-O-O d6 10. f3 Bd7 11. g4 Bc6 12. Nd5 Bxd2+ 13. Qxd2 Bxd5 14. exd5 Rfe8 (14... c6 {Yeo-Staples, British U21 Championship, August 1972}) 15. Bb5 c6 16. Rhe1 Qxd5 17. Rxe8+ Nxe8 18. Qxd5 cxd5 19. Bxe8 Rxe8 20. Rxd5 Re6 21. Kd2 {Sources: CHESS, January 1973, Vol.38/665-6, p120; Dinosaur (Mitcham CC bulletin). CHESS Magazine's comment: "I'll never answer 1 e4 with 1...e5 against an Englishman again!" - Ludek Pachman after the game. Yeo had played the whole game up to about move 19 in a Cambridge inter-college match. (But Michael Yeo later commented: "not true! It followed my game against Staples from the British U21 at Brighton earlier in the year until move 14 when Staples played the worse 14...c6.")} 1/2-1/2

